The exact-primitives proposition proves \(\kappa(c^\dagger)=5/8\).  The Airy-benchmark definition therefore gives
\[
 \Lambda_{c^\dagger}=C_A\kappa(c^\dagger)^{2/3}
 =C_A(5/8)^{2/3}>0,
\tag{14}
\]
where positivity uses the declared range \(C_A\in(0,\infty)\).  Applying the established uniform-risk upper theorem to the permitted three-active-arm contrast \(c^\dagger\) gives
\[
 \liminf_{n\to\infty}n^{4/3}
 \{n^{-1}-R_n(c^\dagger)\}
 \ge \Lambda_{c^\dagger}.
\tag{15}
\]
Combining (14) and (15) proves the narrowed statement.  This argument is attaining-side only: it supplies no reverse inequality, and the exact contradiction (12)--(13) prevents the proposed widening tube from supplying one.
